# These rules were local to one machine in .git/info/exclude, which does not travel with a clone.
# They are tracked now so an agent in a fresh checkout ignores the same things this one does.

# A global ignore on this machine excludes AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md in every repository. The three at
# the root predate it and stayed tracked, so the rule was invisible until it kept
# research/folder-hiding/AGENTS.md out of this repository entirely, while the root AGENTS.md went on
# telling agents to read it first. Instruction files are the contract here, so they come back.
!AGENTS.md
!CLAUDE.md
!GEMINI.md

# Host tooling. nsptool under here is what the nspire MCP invokes, so this does not move. Anchored
# to the root: a bare tools/ matches at any depth and silently swallowed nps/tools/, which cost two
# lanes their new files before a commit refused them. The negations below keep the sources we own.
!/tools/
/tools/*
!/tools/nsptool/
!/tools/keysvc/
/tools/nsptool/*
/tools/keysvc/*
!/tools/nsptool/*.c
!/tools/nsptool/*.py
!/tools/keysvc/*.c
!/tools/keysvc/*.h
!/tools/keysvc/*.py
!/tools/nsptool/tests/
!/tools/keysvc/tests/
/tools/nsptool/tests/*
/tools/keysvc/tests/*
!/tools/nsptool/tests/*.c
!/tools/nsptool/tests/*.py
!/tools/keysvc/tests/*.c
!/tools/keysvc/tests/*.h
!/tools/keysvc/tests/*.py

.DS_Store
.idea/
__pycache__/

# Build outputs, wherever they land. The vendored trees under vendor/ ship .tns and .bin files that
# are the vendored thing itself, so those two extensions are deliberately absent from this list.
*.o
*.a
*.lo
*.la
*.so
*.so.*
*.dylib
*.exe
*.elf
*.gcda
*.gcno

# Emulator boot and flash images, about 12 GB and individually past the 100 MiB GitHub limit. Stays
# at the root: the nspire MCP server hard codes IMAGES_DIR to "images" and resolves boot1.img under
# it, with no override, so moving this takes the emulator down for every lane at once. The tracked
# README beside them records what each base image is and where it came from.
/images/*
!/images/README.md

# Build trees. Anchored so a source directory named build elsewhere is not swallowed.
/nps/build/
/device/

# Scratch and investigation material, none of it built against.
/scratch/
/.Internal/references/
/.ndl-migration-recovery/

# Vendored third-party trees. The upstream sources, licenses and provenance files are tracked. What
# is excluded below is either regenerable or too large for GitHub, so a clone builds it rather than
# carrying it. See vendor-history/README.md for upstreams and the patches carried on top.
/vendor/ndl-src/ndl-sdk/toolchain/download/
/vendor/ndl-src/ndl-sdk/toolchain/install/
/vendor/ndl-src/ndl-sdk/toolchain/build/
/vendor/libnspire-install/
/vendor/*/autom4te.cache/
/vendor/**/.libs/
/vendor/**/.deps/
/vendor/**/config.status
/vendor/**/config.log
/vendor/**/libtool
/vendor/**/*.tar.gz
/vendor/**/*.tar.xz
/vendor/**/*.tar.bz2
/vendor/**/*.tgz
/vendor/firebird-src/headless/firebird-headless

# Upstream carries its own CI. Nothing in this repository runs on push and nothing here should.
/vendor/**/.github/workflows/

# Build trees inside the vendored sources. Everything below is produced by running a build here, so
# a clone rebuilds rather than inheriting objects linked against this machine's toolchain.
/vendor/firebird-src/build-qt5/
/vendor/firebird-src/headless/build/
/vendor/khi-src/micropython-1.12/ports/*/build/
*.dSYM/
/vendor/firebird-src/callback-experiment-0908/callback-test-*
/vendor/firebird-src/callback-experiment-0908/cpu-lifecycle-test
/vendor/firebird-src/callback-experiment-0908/cpu-lifecycle-test-san
/vendor/firebird-src/callback-experiment-0908/ownership-test-*
/vendor/firebird-src/callback-experiment-0908/queued-test-*
/vendor/firebird-src/callback-experiment-0908/reviewer-lifecycle-*
/vendor/firebird-src/callback-experiment-0908/firebird-headless-experiment

# The GMP, MPFR and MPFI sources are vendored as the upstream archives they came in, because the two
# build scripts beside them delete and re-extract these directories on every run. Tracking the
# extracted trees would mean a build leaves thousands of modified files behind in a shared checkout.
/vendor/deps/gmp-6.3.0/
/vendor/deps/mpfr-4.2.2/
/vendor/deps/mpfi-master/
!/vendor/deps/*.tar.gz
!/vendor/deps/*.tar.xz

# The handbook renders. The JSON sources, the reviews and the assets are tracked, and so are the two
# PDFs, which are the form anybody actually reads. HTML and DOCX are 58 MB of the same content.
/docs/nps-manual/*.html
/docs/nps-manual/*.docx

# What configure wrote on this machine. These carry this checkout's absolute paths, so a clone that
# inherited them would drive a toolchain at a path it does not have. The inputs they are generated
# from, Makefile.am, Makefile.in, config.h.in and libnspire.pc.in, stay tracked and reconfigure.
/vendor/libnspire-src/**/Makefile
/vendor/libnspire-src/config.h
/vendor/libnspire-src/libnspire.pc
/vendor/libnspire-src/stamp-h1
/vendor/**/*~

# Vendored EABase, EASTL and etl. The provenance and license files under them are tracked and stay
# tracked, because .gitignore never untracks what is already in the index. Only the headers we
# compile against were vendored, so upstream tests, benchmarks and docs are excluded.
/nps/third_party/EABase/
/nps/third_party/EASTL/
/nps/third_party/etl/

# The folder-hiding prototype's compiled output. Its sources, factory manifests, staging documents
# and test evidence are tracked, because the nested instructions there treat them as recovery
# material rather than as artifacts a build regenerates.
/research/folder-hiding/build/

# Where agents do their work. Everything under here is a lane checkout, a build tree or a scratch
# file, so none of it belongs in a commit. The convention is written up in AGENTS.md.
/.Internal/workspaces/

# Scratch worktrees. Agents run lanes in sibling checkouts of this repo, and a pathspec-less add in
# the shared tree will otherwise sweep another lane's entire worktree into a commit.
/.lane-*/
/.lead-tree*/
/.headcheck/
/.headcheck-*/
/.headcheck-build/
/.headcheck.lock
/.headcheck-selftest-index

# claude-code-runtime
**/.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
**/.claude/scheduled_tasks.json
**/.claude/routines/.state/
**/.claude/worktrees/
**/.claude/checkpoints/
**/.claude/mailbox/
**/.claude/agent-registry.json
**/.claude/agent-memory-local
**/.claude/first-run
**/.claude/assistant-daemon-state.json
